# A try block in the body of a loop adds nothing to a turn that does not throw. The call ends its block, the handler lies behind a rare edge, and the other edge goes on to the addition and the step.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Double b@[[checked]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}Terminal|ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: #[[next]], Rare:#{{*}}
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[next]]:
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK: Int64 b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, $1(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# The function has calls, and Windows passes arguments in other registers: its count is not checked.
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 16, patchpoints: 3, rare instructions: 52
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 15, patchpoints: 3, rare instructions: 53
